# What does NOT go into the image.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, and without this file that means the
# whole checkout — including .git, which is 324 MB of history for an app that
# never reads it. Nothing at runtime shells out to git; the version comes
# from the VERSION file.
#
# This is not tidiness. A build has a disk quota and an image has a size, and
# both were being spent on a copy of every version of every file this project
# has ever had. What the app actually needs is main.py, the pages, the
# corpus, pyodide, and the fonts.
#
# What is NOT excluded, deliberately: corpus.db.gz and corpus-pics.db (the
# NCERT text and the chapter diagrams — the product cannot do what it is sold
# for without them), pyodide/ (the Python lab runs offline), and the vendored
# libraries (pdf.js, pdf-lib, jsPDF, three.js — a school network filters).

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Local development only. Never in the image, and .venv in particular is a
# Windows virtualenv whose binaries would not run in a Linux container.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Secrets never travel in an image layer. .env is gitignored too, so this is
# belt and braces — but an image is passed around more freely than a repo.
.env
.env.*

# The test suite runs before a deploy, not inside the container.
tests/

# Editor, agent and OS leavings.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Sales material and build leftovers.
deckshots/
*.pptx.tmp
cloudflared.exe
